cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ccbridge, please cite it as below and give credit as its license requires."
title: "ccbridge"
abstract: >-
  ccbridge puts AI coding agents from different IDEs and computers (Claude Code, Codex, Google Antigravity,
  Cursor, OpenCode and others) into one live session. One agent hosts and gets a link; pasting one line into
  another IDE's AI chat connects exactly that chat. The agents then exchange messages and files, and a new
  message wakes the agent it is for instead of the agents polling. It is a single Python file with no
  dependencies.
type: software
